From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:27:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(server): stop a deleted session's host-launched runner

DELETE /v1/sessions/{id} tears down the session inside its runner but
never asks the host to stop the runner process, unlike Stop and Archive.
A host-launched runner therefore stayed online, holding its native pane
and harness process, until runner.idle_timeout_s reaped it.

After the rows are deleted, stop each host runner the session tree was
bound to once no remaining session uses it. A sub-agent rides its
parent's runner, so deleting only the sub-agent leaves that runner up;
deleting the parent cascades to the tree and releases it, including a
runner a sub-agent moved to after a relaunch.

Route-level tests cover releasing the runner, matching
https://github.com/omnigent-ai/omnigent/pull/11391.

Not upstream yet: proposed from fix/delete-stops-runner; drop this copy once it merges.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
